// Waiting for Stars: the Liminalia template story. Rewrite it to make it your own.
// The tutorial on the website shows how to write a story (https://liminalia.skyta.dev/en/tutorial/).
// The command reference explains every command (https://liminalia.skyta.dev/en/reference/).
// New Game starts at the top of this file (entry in liminalia.json).
//
// The scenes in this file:
//   start     At dusk, Akari meets Sou at the old observatory
//   night     Night falls. @scene-change changes the scene (the fade time is in commandDefaults in liminalia.json)
//   menu      Choices: the telescope, the radio, or going outside. A variable remembers whether Akari looked through the telescope
//   midnight  The meteor shower. Make a wish, or watch in silence (also kept in a variable)
//   ending    The ending depends on the choices, then the story goes on to the dawn in epilogue.lim
// The radio scene is the voice on the radio. Put the news in a variable, then call the scene with @call.
// Assets are in assets/, and the characters and their sprites are in cast.json (SAMPLE-ASSETS.txt explains the sample assets).

# start
@set game.looked = false
@set game.wished = false
@mask
@bg hill_dusk.webp
@bgm quiet_night.wav volume=60 time=2s
@mask-off time=1500ms
@window show time=300ms
At the top of the slope stands a small observatory.
It has a round roof, and nobody in town uses it anymore.
Tonight, they say, a {i once-in-a-century} meteor shower is coming. {click}At least, that's all the radio has been saying since morning.
@chara Akari normal at=center time=400ms
Akari "Made it! Was this hill always this long?"
Catching my breath, I checked the binoculars in my bag.
@se chime.wav
The little bell hanging on the door jingled, though there wasn't any wind.
@chara Akari surprised at=left time=300ms
@chara Sou normal at=right time=400ms
Sou "Oh, a visitor. That's rare."
Akari "Oh! S-sorry. I wasn't trying to sneak in or anything."
Sou "Come on in. This place doesn't belong to anyone anymore."
@chara Akari normal at=left
The young man said his name was Sou. He had been keeping the keys to the observatory for a long time.
Sou "You came to see the shooting stars, right? {br}Then you're early. The real show starts once the night gets deeper."
Akari "Then could I wait here until it starts?"
@chara Sou smile at=right
Sou "Be my guest. Waiting is what this place does best."

# night
@scene-change hill_night.webp
@chara Akari normal at=left time=400ms
@chara Sou normal at=right time=400ms
Once the sun went down, the hilltop turned into a ceiling of stars.
The lights of the town were far away, and only the observatory window glowed.
Sou "Well, then. What shall we do while we wait?"

# menu
@choice
- Look through the telescope -> #telescope
- Turn on the radio -> #radio_on
- Go outside and look up -> #outside
@end

# telescope
@set game.looked = true
Sou "This telescope is old, but I polish the lens every year."
@chara-hide-all time=300ms
@window hide
@camera zoom=1.6 x=-380 y=-210 time=1500ms ease=easeOutSine
@window show
Through the lens, the edge of the moon looked far more rugged than I had imagined.
Akari "I didn't know the moon was this close."
Sou "It only looks close. {click}Reach out, and it's still far away."
@reset-camera time=1s
@chara Akari smile at=left time=300ms
@chara Sou normal at=right time=300ms
Akari "It's far away, but you can still see it clearly."
@jump #menu

# radio_on
@set temp.news = "Tonight's meteor shower is expected to peak at around midnight."
@call #radio
@chara Akari normal at=left
Akari "See? It keeps saying the same thing."
@chara Sou smile at=right
Sou "Something that keeps telling you the same thing can be a comfort."
@jump #menu

# outside
@chara-hide Sou time=300ms
@chara Akari normal at=center time=300ms
When I stepped outside, the night wind was cold on my cheeks.
The sky above was so wide that I had no idea where the shooting stars would come from.
@se gust.wav
@quake time=500ms count=4 horizontal=8 vertical=3
@chara Akari surprised at=center
A sudden gust rattled the observatory door.
Akari "Whoa, whoa...!"
@chara Akari surprised at=left time=300ms
@chara Sou normal at=right time=300ms
Sou "The wind on this hill sometimes arrives before the stars. {br}...It's almost time."

# midnight
@set temp.news = "It is now midnight. The meteor shower is about to reach its peak."
@call #radio
@chara Akari normal at=left
Akari "It's starting...!"
@chara-hide-all time=500ms
@window hide
@camera zoom=1.3 y=-100 time=2s ease=easeOutSine
@mask color=#ffffff time=150ms
@mask-off time=600ms
@window show
{speed 90ms One, then another.}{br}All over the sky, thin streaks of light drew lines and vanished.
Forgetting to breathe, I tried to count them, and gave up almost at once.
@reset-camera time=1500ms
@chara Akari smile at=left time=400ms
@chara Sou smile at=right time=400ms
Sou "Make a wish three times before a shooting star fades. That's what they say, isn't it?"
Akari "Three times? No way. {click}{@chara Akari surprised at=left}They're way too fast!"
@chara Sou normal at=right
Sou "That's why everyone keeps their wishes short. ...What about you?"
@choice
- Try making a wish -> #wish
- Watch in silence -> #watch
@end

# wish
@set game.wished = true
@chara Akari normal at=left
Akari "Um... 'I hope I can come back here again!'"
@chara Sou surprised at=right
Sou "...Did you really say that three times?"
@chara Akari smile at=left
Akari "Only once. But I said it really loud, so I'm sure it was heard."
@jump #ending

# watch
@set game.wished = false
@chara Akari normal at=left
I didn't say anything. I just followed the light with my eyes.
While I was still thinking of a wish, the stars faded first.
Sou "That's fine too. {br}Just watching is enough to remember it."

# ending
@if game.wished && game.looked
When the shooting stars had thinned out, Sou placed the telescope's lens cap in my palm.
Sou "Would you come back next year to polish the lens? On my own, I tend to cut corners."
@chara Akari smile at=left
Akari "Yes. It's a promise."
@elif game.wished
When the shooting stars had thinned out, Sou took one of the bells off the door and let me hold it.
Sou "If you come back, just ring this. I'll know right away."
@else
When the shooting stars had thinned out, Sou said nothing, and only left the door open a little.
Sou "I'll leave this door open."
@end
@stop-bgm time=2s
@jump epilogue

// The radio. Put the news to read in temp.news, then @call this scene.
# radio
@se radio.wav channel=1
@wait 600ms
Radio "This is the hill town radio station. {br}{= temp.news}"
@stop-se channel=1 time=300ms
@return
